Basic Inventory System
Objective:
• Implement a basic inventory system where items can be collected and managed.
Description: This script manages the player’s inventory, allowing item collection and
display.
here step by step by step:-
🔹 Step 1: Create a New Unity Project

Open Unity Hub

Click New Project

Select 2D (or 3D) template

Name it: BasicInventorySystem

Click Create

🔹 Step 2: Create UI Text for Inventory Display
(For Unity 2021+ using Canvas)

In Hierarchy

Right-click → UI → Canvas

Right-click on Canvas

UI → Text – TextMeshPro

If asked, click Import TMP Essentials

Rename

Rename Text object to InventoryText

Set Text Properties

Text: Inventory:

Font Size: 24–30

Alignment: Top Left

Position it on screen using Rect Transform

🔹 Step 3: Create Inventory Script

In Project Window

Right-click → Create → C# Script

Name it: InventorySystem

Double-click and paste this code 👇

using UnityEngine;
using TMPro;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class InventorySystem : MonoBehaviour
{
    public TextMeshProUGUI inventoryText;
    private List<string> inventory = new List<string>();

    void Start()
    {
        UpdateInventoryUI();
    }

    void UpdateInventoryUI()
    {
        inventoryText.text = "Inventory: " + string.Join(", ", inventory);
    }

    public void AddItem(string item)
    {
        inventory.Add(item);
        UpdateInventoryUI();
    }
}


✅ Important Changes

Used TextMeshProUGUI

Added System.Collections.Generic

🔹 Step 4: Attach Script to GameObject

In Hierarchy

Right-click → Create Empty

Rename it InventoryManager

Drag InventorySystem.cs onto InventoryManager

🔹 Step 5: Link UI Text to Script

Click InventoryManager

In Inspector

Drag InventoryText from Hierarchy into:
👉 Inventory Text field

🔹 Step 6: Add Item Using Button (Test Method)
Create Button

Right-click Canvas

UI → Button – TextMeshPro

Rename Button: AddItemButton

Change Button text to: Add Item

Button Click Setup

Select AddItemButton

In Inspector → OnClick()

Click +

Drag InventoryManager into empty field

Choose:

InventorySystem → AddItem(string)


Type item name:

Sword

🔹 Step 7: Run the Scene ▶️

Click Play

Press Add Item button

Output:

Inventory: Sword


Click again:

Inventory: Sword, Sword


🎉 Inventory System Working Successfully!

